{
 "about": "Who enters at a posting of the MBA role set: an MBA graduate (\"mba\"), a bachelor's or non-MBA master's graduate (\"pre_mba\"), or neither (null, an experienced-hire job or no evidence). Read by pipeline/roles_mba.py (entry()) and written into web/data/roles_mba.json under \"entry\". Levels are not changed by this table. Every pattern is a JavaScript regular expression used with the \"i\" flag. A firm row is tested on the title after the firm's own first word is removed, first match wins. \"basis\": \"primary\" = the firm's own posting or page says it; \"secondary\" = a guide, a forum, a page of another office or an inference. Facts come from the research note of 2026-10-12 (evals/NOTES.md, \"Entry mark\"). What a source means: \"title\" and \"text\" say the posting itself is written for that audience; \"firm\" and \"category\" say the title is the grade at which that audience joins (the posting may also be open to experienced hires).",
